# The snapshot of each multi-image demo with a development route on Forgejo,
# in one scratch repository each: the demo's main and a change on branch
# development, then the harness's service development workflow dispatched on
# main, which snapshots development through the snapshot-images policy. The
# trial judges the frozen plan and every planned image's receipt, the plan
# the snapshot planner makes of the declaration the demo's release builds
# its images from, overlaid native linux/amd64 and unsigned; a case names no
# image. The snapshot event probes no readiness, even for one image: image
# count does not declare a runnable service. Nothing is released. A demo the
# snapshot cannot plan, or without
# the Forgejo release workflow the harness's workflow is pinned by, is
# refused before anything is created (docs/live-campaigns.md, Snapshot).
# hello-monorepo ships no Forgejo workflows, so it has no line here.
# The builder is the line's CI_IMAGE_BUILDER, Buildah on the contract's
# runner that permits user namespaces; leave
# FORGE_CI_LIVE_FORGEJO_IMAGE_BUILDER unset. The visibility is the run's:
# FORGE_CI_LIVE_CONSUMER_VISIBILITY unset or both runs each line public and
# private. Prepare with forgejo=<this file> and
# job-image=rust:<reviewed local image>; CI_JOB_IMAGE is the image the
# snapshot builds the demo's producers in, none for the container-first
# Cargo workspace. amd64 runners only for now. A selector reruns one line:
#
#   just campaign-lane <dir> forgejo test/live/campaigns/snapshot-forgejo.cases
#   just campaign-lane <dir> forgejo test/live/campaigns/snapshot-forgejo.cases hello-cargo-workspace/snapshot/image-builder=buildah/visibility=public

consumer hello-cargo-workspace snapshot CI_JOB_IMAGE=@JOB_IMAGE_RUST CI_IMAGE_BUILDER=buildah
